-- title:
--   Order of the finite p^v-torsion of J_H(M) at p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image under reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, and a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $Pl$ and with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$. Assume the $q$-expansion $j$-series `jqModC` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC` of ratios of integral $q$-expansions of level-$\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ modular forms, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport-type integral model datum `XHDRModelAtP` for level $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $R_p$, let $\Lambda$ be level data at $Pl$ for the auxiliary level $\Gamma_N$ (a scheme with relative group law over $\operatorname{Spec} R_p$ together with identifications of its generic and special sections with $J_H(M/p)$ and with the degree-zero class group over $\kappa$), and let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP`: a smooth separated quasi-compact surjective relative group scheme $g : G \to \operatorname{Spec} R_p$ with commutative relative group law, a Galois- and Hecke-equivariant bijection $\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_H(M)$ onto its generic sections, and a toric rank `toricRank`. Assume further that the designation built from $(O.G, O.g)$ and the identity section of its group law represents the relative Picard subfunctor cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero for the level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ model rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\infty}$, and that the designation built from $\Lambda$ represents the corresponding subfunctor for the level-$\Gamma_N$ model rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\infty}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$. Then for every $v \in \mathbb{N}$ the group generated by those $p^v$-torsion classes in the degree-zero class group of the level-$H$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose associated generic section of $g$ extends to a section over $Pl$ has cardinality $p^{v(t + 4g')}$, where $t = O.\mathrm{toricRank}$ and $g'$ is the genus `genusFF` over $\kappa$ of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H'}(M/p)$, $H'$ the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$.
--
--   This is the counting of the finite part of the $p^v$-torsion of the Jacobian $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$ in the case $p \parallel M$, where the special fibre is semistable with toric rank $t$ and abelian part of dimension $2g'$. It feeds the computation of torsion orders and the production of suitable torsion points used in the level-lowering step.
